# Local test workflow

When the user runs **`/test`**, asks to test this repository, expand coverage, or verify frontend-backend linkage:

1. Read the skill: project `.cursor/skills/adversarial-documentation-driven-testing/SKILL.md` (symlink to master) or `~/.cursor/skills/adversarial-documentation-driven-testing/SKILL.md` (same files).
2. Follow `.cursor/commands/test.md` in **this project** when present; otherwise `~/.cursor/commands/test.md`.
3. Phase 2 of `/test` **must** run `/coverage` (`.cursor/commands/coverage.md`) and loop test expansion until statement, branch, and condition coverage are all ≥ 80% on measured modules (or a dated exception exists), then present `artifacts/coverage-report.md`.
4. Run `make adversarial-preflight` from **this repo root** (not only `../webtools-ui`) before product suites.
5. Do not skip preflight because a sibling checkout also has the skill.
